A||||5||GodSend||Power Wire?||||6||
Z||000000||GodSend||01-29-2001||06:50 PM||||Hey guys,<P>Im looking for advice on how to route a 4 gauge power wite from the battery (still in the back) to the inside of the car, thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-29-2001||07:02 PM||||run it along the top of firewall from battery, if you cant find a hole in center to go into the back of center console, you can drill one. A main harness goes thru there, i put a radio antenna thru it. If you have to drill one remember the computer and gas tank are both there too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GodSend||01-30-2001||11:01 AM||||Speaking of drilling.  My amp install will require me to drill a few screws into the firewall (2 or 3 on each side)  This will be on the lower part of the firewall, is there anything I should look out for in there?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-30-2001||11:14 AM||||My power wire runs under the battery case. If you remove the passenger side carpet you'll see a seam. approx 2" above the seam is where I drilled. This puts the hole below the battery case and above the brake line. (Always check before drilling)(always use a rubber grommet) As for the amp, below the seam is the false panel. You can mount the amp into that. On the drivers side the fuel filler tube is behind it in the upper right corner.||||reg||1
Z||000004||varnster||01-30-2001||09:15 PM||||if you take losen your computer from the rear<BR>fire wall behind it is a huge rubber gromet<BR>that is not used, it will be tight but I think you could fit that garden hose through<BR>it and behind the computer, give it a try before cutting your car. its behind the plastic holder the computer mounts to.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-30-2001||09:25 PM||||I always try to keep my power and grounds away from the computer and engine control wires. Less chance of noise inducted into the wires.||||reg||1
